#: temp.glade:28878
msgid "For commonly used series of illustrations, PTXprint\n"
"can automatically generate the appropriate copyright\n"
"attribution statement(s) as part of the colophon text.\n\n"
"For other less-known artists' you may enter the appropriate\n"
"copyright information which is usually in the format of:\n"
"   by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type."
msgstr "Long ol piksa ol i save yusim planti taim, PTXprint inap kamapim aut ol rait bilong ol man i gat rait long wokim ol piksa olsem hap bilong ol rait bilong ol piksa."

#: temp.glade:28886
msgid "Copyright\n"
"Attribution:"
msgstr "Tok bilong ol man i raitim:"

#: temp.glade:28897
msgid "Picture: Copyright attribution"
msgstr "Piksa: Toksave long rait"

#: temp.glade:28900
msgid "There are several shortcuts you can use:\n"
"   (c) --> ©  the copyright sign\n"
"   (r) --> ®  to denote registered trademarks\n"
"   (tm) --> ™  to denote trademarks in general"
msgstr "Yu ken yusim sampela liklik rot: (c) --> © rait bilong rait (r) --> ® bilong makim ol mak ol i bin rejistaim (tm) --> TM bilong makim ol mak olgeta"

#: temp.glade:28905
msgid "by Artist Name © Year, Entity Name and License Type"
msgstr "Long nem bilong Artist © Year, Entity Name and License Type"

#: temp.glade:28918
msgid "The frame size determines how large the picture\n"
"will appear on the page.\n\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"When using single column layout, there is no\n"
"difference between Column Width and Span Width."
msgstr "Long pes bilong buk, bikpela piksa i makim bikpela piksa bai kamap long pes. Long pes bilong buk, bikpela piksa i save stap antap o daun tasol. Long pes bilong buk, bikpela piksa i gat sampela narapela samting i stap antap o daun. Long pes bilong buk, bikpela piksa i gat sampela narapela samting i stap daunbilo."

#: temp.glade:28941
msgid "Several options here are extensions to the normal USFM\n"
"markup standard for illustrations and are not expected\n"
"to work in other software. But PTXprint allows a greater\n"
"level of control in placing pictures.\n\n"
"Top: Above everything except the header line\n"
"Bottom: Below all verse text (and footnotes in diglot)\n"
"Before Verse: 'Here' where defined or before its Anchor Ref\n"
"After Paragraph: After this paragraph\n"
"Cutout: A notch/corner cut out of the text, starting at current line\n\n"
"The above options may have other positioning parameters such\n"
"as: Left, Right, Center, no. of lines (up or down)."
msgstr "Sampela opesen i stap hia em ol ekstension bilong ol markup standard bilong USFM bilong ol piksa na ol i no inap wok long ol narapela program. Antap: Antap long olgeta samting, tasol long het rait Bottom: Antap long olgeta ves rait (na ol tok daunbilo long tupela hap) Paslain long Ves: 'Here' we i gat mak o paslain long Anchor Ref After Paragraph: Bihain long dispela paragraf Cutout: Wanpela notch/kok bilong rait, stat long dispela lain Opsion antap inap gat ol narapela sait bilong putim ol samting olsem: Left, Right, Center, no. bilong ol lain (up o down)."

#: temp.glade:28966
msgid "Picture: Scale"
msgstr "Piksa: Skala"

#: temp.glade:28969
msgid "An image (illustration) can be scaled to the\n"
"given size. This is particularly useful for\n"
"cutout images, and can prevent them from\n"
"taking up too much space within the text."
msgstr "Ol piksa (olsem piksa) inap kamap bikpela olsem ol piksa i stap long en. Dispela i gutpela tru long ol piksa i stap long ol piksa ol i katim, na dispela inap pasim ol long kisim planti hap bilong ol piksa insait long ol tok."

#: temp.glade:28988
msgid "Picture: Vertical position"
msgstr "Piksa: Ples i sanap stret"

#: temp.glade:28993
msgid "Several options here are extensions to the normal USFM\n"
"markup standard for illustrations and are not expected\n"
"to work in other software. But PTXprint allows a greater\n"
"level of control in placing pictures.\n\n"
"Top: Above everything except the header line\n"
"Bottom: Below all verse text (and footnotes in diglot)\n"
"Below Notes: Below the footnotes (Span Width only)\n"
"Before Verse: 'Here' where defined or before its Anchor Ref\n"
"After Paragraph: After this paragraph\n"
"Cutout: A notch/corner cut out of the text, starting at current line\n\n"
"The above options may have other positioning parameters such\n"
"as: Left, Right, Center, no. of lines (up or down)."
msgstr ""

#: temp.glade:29031
msgid "Picture: Frame size"
msgstr "Piksa: Mak bilong piksa"

#: temp.glade:29036
msgid "The frame size determines the boundaries of where the\n"
"picture will appear on the page.\n\n"
"Span Width only allows a Top or Bottom vertical placement.\n\n"
"Column Width allows several other more precise placement \n"
"options: Before Verse, After Paragraph, or Cutout; and these\n"
"can have Left/Inner or Right/Outer Horizontal positioning set. \n"
" \n"
"Page (in Margins) is intended for pictures that will cover an\n"
"entire page (i.e. preventing any scripture text from being on\n"
"that page), but will still show the header.\n\n"
"Page (to Edge) is intended for pictures (or more commonly\n"
"for maps) to fill the entire page, with no margins at all. \n"
"Captions should not be used with 'Page (to Edge)' images."
msgstr "Long dispela pes, ol i makim wanem hap piksa bai kamap long en. Long pes bilong piksa, ol i makim hap piksa bai kamap long en. Long pes bilong piksa, ol i makim hap piksa bai kamap long en. Long pes bilong piksa, ol i makim hap piksa bai kamap long en. Long pes bilong piksa, ol i makim hap piksa bai kamap long en. Long pes bilong piksa, ol i makim hap piksa bai kamap long en. Ol piksa i stap long pes (olsem page to edge) i bilong ol piksa (o planti taim ol mep) i ken pulapim olgeta pes, na i no gat wanpela mak bilong en."

#: temp.glade:29095
msgid "Picture: Horizontal position"
msgstr "Piksa: Ples bilong ol samting"

#: temp.glade:29129
msgid "It is good typesetting practice to make people\n"
"look outwards from the gutter, so you can set\n"
"whether the image is to be mirrored just on \n"
"odd pages or even pages.\n\n"
"Some artists' pictures do not take into account\n"
"the \"dirty left-hand\" culture. For example, it would\n"
"be \"awkward\" to use a picture where Jesus is healing\n"
"a person using his LEFT hand! What an insult!\n\n"
"So this option allows the image to be mirrored (on\n"
"both pages) in order to make the left become right.\n"
"But you should check carefully to see what other\n"
"unwanted side effects this mirroring may cause.\n\n"
"Note: This option will be grayed out if the picture has  \n"
"the \"Never Mirror\" setting checked on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "Sampela piksa bilong ol man bilong wokim piksa i no tingim pasin bilong \"longlong han kais\". Olsem: Sapos piksa i soim Jisas i mekim wok long han kais bilong em long oraitim sik bilong wanpela man, dispela bai \"mekim yu bel hevi\". Toksave: Dispela senis bai kamap gray sapos piksa i gat mak \"No ken Lukim Ol Samting Long Mirror\" long tab \"Lukim Ol Samting Long Mirror\"."

#: temp.glade:29147
msgid "Mirror:"
msgstr "Ol piksa:"

#: temp.glade:29158
msgid "Picture: Mirroring options"
msgstr "Piksa: Ol rot bilong soim piksa"

#: temp.glade:29162
msgid "Never = The image will never be mirrored\n"
"Odd = Mirrored only if image ends up on an odd page\n"
"Even = Mirrored only if image ends up on an even page\n"
"Always = Always mirrored (regardless of where it ends up)\n\n"
"Note that if this option is grayed out, it is because \n"
"you have already restricted the mirroring options \n"
"on the Checklist tab."
msgstr "No ken = Ol i no ken mekim piksa i kamap long narapela pes Odd = Ol i no mekim piksa i kamap long narapela pes Even = Ol i no mekim piksa i kamap long narapela pes Always = Ol i save mekim piksa i kamap long narapela pes Always = Ol i save mekim piksa i kamap long narapela pes (olsem wanem hap piksa i kamap long en) Tingim olsem sapos dispela opesen i stap gray, dispela i kamap long wanem, yu bin pasim pinis ol opesen bilong mekim piksa i kamap long narapela pes Checklist tab."

#: temp.glade:29197 temp.glade:29224
msgid "Some vertical position options allow a picture\n"
"to be moved up or down by a number of lines\n"
"or paragraphs.\n\n"
"-Negative (minus) values specify to move UP.\n"
"+Positive (plus) values specify to move DOWN.\n\n"
"Negative counts for cutouts raise the image,\n"
"but the cutout will not affect earlier paragraphs. \n"
"Note that negative and fractional paragraph \n"
"counts are invalid."
msgstr "Sampela rot bilong putim piksa long het i makim olsem piksa i mas go antap o daun long sampela lain o paragraf. -Negative (minus) values i makim olsem piksa i mas go antap. +Positive (plus) values i makim olsem piksa i mas go daun. Negative count bilong ol cut out i save mekim piksa i go antap, tasol cut out i no inap mekim sampela senis long ol paragraf i stap paslain long dispela."

#: temp.glade:29221
msgid "Picture: Lines to adjust vertically"
msgstr "Piksa: Ol lain i mas bihainim stret"

#: temp.glade:29276
msgid "Can be used in Print/PDF publications. "
msgstr "Ol inap yusim long ol nius ol i prinim/PDF. "

#: temp.glade:29292
